[[15,1,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Before removing and refitting\nthe control unit, carry out the following preliminary operations.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Place the ignition key in the OFF position and extract it;</p><p>Disconnect the battery.</p>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2429604\">7040L40</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429644\">7050A20</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429642\">7050A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429597\">7040H50</a></p><p>1. Working inside the front seat belt pretensioner compartment,\nmove the belt slightly.</p><p>2. Undo the bolt</p><p>3. Move sensor (3a) slightly, release reference pin (3a) from its\nseat and disconnect electrical connection (3b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Sensor for driver&#x27;s, Side Bag</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/2428522\">K66</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Sensor for driver&#x27;s, Side Bag</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/2428524\">K67</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>4. Recover the sensor.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045096.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the side Air Bag\nsensor is not damaged.</p><p>1. Connect the electrical connection.</p><p>2. Position the Side Bag sensor (2a) in its housing.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The pin (2b) should fit in the\nhole (2c) on the pillar.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Tighten the bolt.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045097.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<p><a href=\"#/2429597\">7040H50</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429642\">7050A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429644\">7050A20</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429604\">7040L40</a></p>"]]